commit bf4a95370f455ac5fdf33c1e44a0e46c5e1323c7
Author: Cassie Spiral <166543307+angelsbrood@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Wed Aug 5 16:34:35 2026 -0700

    Stand down from MTP speculation before the sliding cache wraps (#506)
    
    Stand down MTP speculation before the sliding cache wraps
    
    Once a stream's context crosses the sliding window, `RotatingKVCache` becomes permanently untrimmable, but the iterator only checked `canTrimPromptCache` once at init. Streams that crossed the window kept drafting until the verify pass's sliding K/V exceeded `maxCacheSize`, tripping the `slidingKvLen` precondition in `draftBlock`.
    
    Fix: add `standDownIfNoTrimHeadroom(positions:reason:)`, called at the end of `init` and at the top of each speculative round, which switches to the existing sticky-passthrough regime once the cache can no longer absorb a round and still be rewound. It checks headroom rather than the wrap itself, since the wrap happens inside the verify pass and a post-hoc check would let the boundary round run and silently no-op its rewind.
    
    Also reordered `next()` to drain `pendingTokens` before checking `passthrough`, so an init-time stand-down still yields the prefill bonus.
    
    Untouched: the precondition, `updateConcat`'s overflow allowance, the emit hook, and the classic `SpeculativeDecoding` path.
    
    Added three regression tests plus an opt-in `wrapAt:` on `CountingKVCache` mirroring `RotatingKVCache`'s trim behavior (defaults to nil, no effect on existing tests).
    
    Also documents the sliding-window bound on both public MTP entry points, and moves predictive trim checks into `KVCache`.

