commit 26f3a48f37a0d990f81822fca263408245f0957b
Author: xocialize <dustin.nielson@gmail.com>
Date:   Tue Aug 4 09:47:49 2026 -0700

    Add custom LogitProcessor injection to GenerateParameters / ChatSession (#401)
    
    Add custom LogitProcessor injection via GenerationComponents
    
    Add support for injecting a custom LogitProcessor (e.g. grammar-constrained decoding) into parameters-driven generation paths (ChatSession, speculative decoding, etc.), which previously only worked via direct TokenIterator construction.
    
    - Introduce `GenerationComponents`, a Sendable struct holding an optional `@Sendable logitProcessorFactory`. Its `logitProcessor(parameters:)` composes the built-in `PenaltyProcessor` with the custom processor via a new public `ChainedLogitProcessor`, matching Python mlx-lm ordering. The factory produces a fresh processor per generation to avoid state leakage across turns.
    - Thread an additive `components: GenerationComponents = .init()` through `TokenIterator`, `SpeculativeTokenIterator`, `MTPSpeculativeTokenIterator`, `ChatSession`, and the parameters-driven `generate`/`generateTokens` functions. `GenerateParameters` itself stays a pure value type (an earlier approach stored the factory there directly; reworked per maintainer feedback). Non-breaking: empty components reproduce prior behavior.
    - Add tests for fresh-instance-per-call/per-generation, empty-components regression, and end-to-end ChatSession masking-processor behavior.
    - Fix DocC symbol links across the repo broken by the new `components:` parameter, verified clean under `--warnings-as-errors`.

