commit 45693f64c9031cdfa65399ea528d6122d1671c67
Author: Christopher Webb <207731778+thechriswebb@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Mon Jul 27 17:30:06 2026 -0400

    Fix guided generation dropping required properties via streaming detokenizer (#465)
    
    NaiveStreamingDetokenizer.next() computed each incremental delta as newSegment.suffix(newSegment.count - segment.count), a character-count diff that assumes decode() is append-only. SentencePiece decoding is not: appending a token can rewrite earlier whitespace (e.g. Gemma decodes [\n, "  "] as "\n  " but [\n, "  ", ","] as "\n ,", collapsing a space), so the count-based suffix computed suffix(0) and silently dropped the newly decoded character. In guided generation that dropped character was a structural JSON comma: the grammar committed every token and stayed valid, but the streamed text was invalid JSON, so FoundationModels failed to decode a required property ("GeneratedContent does not contain a property"). This is why Gemma (SentencePiece) hit it and Qwen (byte-level BPE, append-only) never did.
    
    Fix: diff by common prefix instead of character count. Identical to the old behavior for append-only tokenizers; for non-append-only decodes it never drops characters. As a bonus this also removes a latent scalar-vs-grapheme hazard, since commonPrefix/count/dropFirst all operate on grapheme clusters. A comment documents that correctness relies on the already-emitted prefix being stable (true for SentencePiece, which only collapses whitespace at the append boundary).
    
    Tests: model-free StreamingDetokenizerTests covering the comma-drop regression, an append-only no-change guard, split-multibyte partial-decode (\u{fffd}) emission, and the newline-reset path with a non-append-only decode. Plus an env-gated end-to-end regression (RequiredPropertyStressTests, MLX_RUN_REQUIRED_PROPERTY_STRESS): 0/25 failures with the fix, was 3/15 before.

diff --git a/IntegrationTesting/IntegrationTestingTests/MLXFoundationModelsIntegration/GuidedGeneration/RequiredPropertyStressTests.swift b/IntegrationTesting/IntegrationTestingTests/MLXFoundationModelsIntegration/GuidedGeneration/RequiredPropertyStressTests.swift
new file mode 100644
